# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Large binaries and derived artifacts. results/ IS committed (PLAN.md §13):
# results/*/grid.csv, results/*/report.md and results/*.md are the reported
# deliverables and must stay readable on GitHub.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Datasets (~1 GB) are never committed. NOTE: this is "data/*" and not "data/"
# on purpose -- a bare directory pattern stops git descending into data/, which
# makes the negations below impossible.
data/*
!data/.gitkeep
!data/manifests/
data/manifests/*
!data/manifests/.gitkeep

# The forbidden-subset blocklist IS committed: 490 KB, and without it the
# PLAN.md section 4.3.2 assertions pass vacuously on a fresh clone. Rebuilding
# it means re-downloading COCO val2017 (797 MB), which the zip rule below keeps
# out of the repo.
!data/forbidden/
data/forbidden/*
!data/forbidden/blocklist.json

runs/*
results/**/cache/

# Drive exports pulled back from Colab runs: raw feature caches (~150 MB of
# .npy) plus a duplicate of results/. Only the results/ and runs/ files worth
# keeping are copied out by hand; the export tree itself never lands in git.
aigc-phase5/

# Transformed-image cache written by src/evaluate.py --cache-dir
.cache_transforms/

*.npy
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.zip
*.parquet

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.venv/
venv/

.env
.DS_Store

# The three trained checkpoints ARE committed, same reasoning as data/forbidden/
# above: they're the linear head only (~4 KB each; the CLIP backbone downloads
# from open_clip's own registry at runtime), and without them predict.py and
# app.py need a Colab run before anyone can use either. runs/fusion.pt is the
# Phase 5 head -- not wired into either entry point, committed so that
# results/fusion/ can be reproduced.
!runs/baseline.pt
!runs/aug.pt
!runs/fusion.pt
